# TAK-PluginSuite-FeatureLink — repository-wide line-ending and diff policy.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS EXPLICIT (audit Appendix E §2.2 / C-13 cluster)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The previous content was a single bare `* text=auto`. That leaves the checkout
# end-of-line to each contributor's `core.autocrlf`, so on a Windows workstation git
# rewrites LF-committed Java/XML/TypeScript sources to CRLF in the working tree and
# emits `LF will be replaced by CRLF` on every `git add`. The practical harm is not
# the warning: it is that a contributor whose editor then saves the file back produces
# a whole-file diff, and a one-line substantive change becomes invisible inside a
# 400-line whitespace diff.
#
# CORRECT END STATE FOR THIS REPOSITORY
# -------------------------------------
# This suite spans four toolchains with genuinely different requirements:
#
#   * Android / Gradle (ATAK5.6, ATAK5.7)  — LF. `gradlew` is a POSIX shell script and
#     must be LF or it will not execute on a Linux CI runner.
#   * Windows / .NET / WPF (WinTAK5.6, WinTAK5.7) — CRLF-TOLERANT. MSBuild, Roslyn and
#     Visual Studio all read LF sources without complaint, so LF is safe for .cs/.xaml.
#     Only the files Visual Studio itself rewrites (`.sln`) and the Windows shells
#     (`.bat`, `.cmd`, `.ps1`) are pinned to CRLF, because those *are* CRLF-sensitive
#     in practice (cmd.exe mis-parses a trailing bare LF in some batch constructs).
#   * Node / TypeScript (CloudTAK, TAK Portal) — LF.
#   * Python / Flask (Infra-TAK) — LF.
#
# And the load-bearing case: TAK Portal and Infra-TAK are BOTH installed by a shell
# script (`TAKPortal/install.sh`, `Infra-TAK/install.sh`). A `.sh` file checked out with
# CRLF fails on Linux with `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M` — the installer simply does not
# run. `*.sh text eol=lf` below is therefore a correctness requirement, not a preference.
#
# Net rule: LF in the repository and LF on checkout everywhere, with a short, explicit
# CRLF allowlist for Windows-only shells and solution files.
#
# AFTER CHANGING THIS FILE run, in an isolated commit with a clean tree:
#     git add --renormalize .
# so that any file already stored with the wrong endings is corrected once, rather than
# drifting into an unrelated feature diff.

# ── Default: detect text, store LF, check out LF ─────────────────────────────
* text=auto eol=lf

# ── Windows-only files that must stay CRLF ───────────────────────────────────
*.bat     text eol=crlf
*.cmd     text eol=crlf
*.ps1     text eol=crlf
*.psm1    text eol=crlf
*.sln     text eol=crlf
*.vcxproj text eol=crlf
*.props   text eol=crlf
*.targets text eol=crlf

# ── Files that MUST be LF or they do not execute on Linux ────────────────────
# TAKPortal/install.sh, TAKPortal/uninstall.sh, Infra-TAK/install.sh,
# Infra-TAK/uninstall.sh, CloudTAK/install.sh, ATAK5.{6,7}/gradlew
*.sh      text eol=lf
gradlew   text eol=lf
*.bash    text eol=lf

# ── Source: declared text so `text=auto` heuristics can never mis-detect ─────
*.java    text diff=java
*.kt      text diff=java
*.cs      text diff=csharp
*.xaml    text
*.ts      text
*.tsx     text
*.js      text
*.mjs     text
*.cjs     text
*.vue     text
*.py      text diff=python
*.json    text
*.jsonc   text
*.xml     text
*.yml     text
*.yaml    text
*.md      text diff=markdown
*.gradle  text
*.pro     text
*.properties text
*.ejs     text
*.html    text
*.css     text
*.svg     text
*.txt     text
*.cfg     text
*.toml    text
.gitattributes text
.gitignore     text

# ── Binary: never diffed, never end-of-line converted ────────────────────────
# The 14,900 tracked PNGs in particular MUST be marked binary; a `text=auto`
# misdetection on a PNG whose header bytes look textual would corrupt the file.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
*.webp    binary
*.pdf     binary
*.jar     binary
*.aar     binary
*.war     binary
*.class   binary
*.dex     binary
*.apk     binary
*.aab     binary
*.wpk     binary
*.zip     binary
*.7z      binary
*.gz      binary
*.tar     binary
*.dll     binary
*.exe     binary
*.pdb     binary
*.so      binary
*.dylib   binary
*.nupkg   binary
*.snk     binary
*.pfx     binary
*.jks     binary
*.keystore binary
*.ttf     binary
*.otf     binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary

# ── Generated / vendored: collapse in PR diffs and exclude from language stats
# The icon corpora are 7,461 files each and are duplicated across two components
# (see docs/remediation/wp5-crosscutting.md). Marking them linguist-vendored keeps
# GitHub from reporting this as an image repository, and `-diff` keeps a bulk icon
# refresh from rendering 3,600 binary-diff stanzas in a review.
TAKPortal/assets/featurelink-configurator/icons/**  linguist-vendored -diff
Infra-TAK/featurelink_displayconfig_assets/icons/** linguist-vendored -diff

# manifest.json is 203 KB of generated index; it is text and must diff, but it should
# not dominate a review. Reviewers should read the generator change, not the output.
TAKPortal/assets/featurelink-configurator/icons/manifest.json  text linguist-generated
Infra-TAK/featurelink_displayconfig_assets/icons/manifest.json text linguist-generated

# ── Excluded from release archives produced by `git archive` ─────────────────
# `git archive` is the supported way to produce a delivery bundle (a plain directory
# copy would sweep in ATAK5.{6,7}/local.properties, which carry developer paths and
# the keystore password — audit Appendix E §1.2).
FEATURELINK-AUDIT-CHECKLIST.md export-ignore
QUESTIONS-FOR-OWNER.md          export-ignore
docs/remediation/               export-ignore
docs/REMEDIATION-BRIEF.md       export-ignore
.github/                        export-ignore
.gitattributes                  export-ignore
.gitignore                      export-ignore
